{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hxvine1jvVmXFF52HtqLWs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd079-base32\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/base32: Base32 Encode and Decode\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship base32. Scripts that encode or decode Base32 data using the GNU\n6\t  base32 format must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match\n7\t  the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gbase32, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n8\t  all flag combinations, using encoding/base32 from the Go standard library, verified\n9\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Encode stdin or file contents to Base32 and write to stdout.\n13\t  - G2: Decode Base32-encoded input back to binary with --decode (-d).\n14\t  - G3: Support line wrapping control with --wrap (-w).\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gbase32 via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Encoding\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given) and encode the input using RFC 4648 Base32, writing the result to stdout.\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: Must wrap encoded output at 76 characters per line by default.\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: \"-w COLS or --wrap=COLS must set the wrap column. -w 0 disables wrapping (single line output).\"\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: Must exit 1 when a named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr.\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Decoding\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"-d or --decode must decode Base32 input from FILE or stdin and write the binary result to stdout.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: Must ignore whitespace (newlines, spaces) in the input during decoding.\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"-i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters in the input during decoding.\"\n39\t      - R2.4:\n40\t          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr when the input contains invalid Base32 characters (without --ignore-garbage).\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: Must exit 0 on successful encoding or decoding.\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid input, missing file, invalid option).\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n51\t\n52\tnon_goals:\n53\t  - cmd/base32 does not implement Base32hex (extended hex alphabet).\n54\t  - cmd/base32 does not implement Base64; use base64 for that.\n55\t\n56\tpackage_contract:\n57\t  imports:\n58\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\n59\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n60\t\n61\tacceptance_criteria:\n62\t  - id: AC1\n63\t    criterion: \"echo hello | base32 produces Base32 encoded output matching gbase32.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.1\n66\t      - R1.2\n67\t  - id: AC2\n68\t    criterion: \"echo NBSWY3DP | base32 -d produces 'hello', matching gbase32 -d.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R2.1\n71\t      - R2.2\n72\t  - id: AC3\n73\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gbase32 passes for all required test cases.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R2.3\n82\t      - R2.4\n83\t  - id: AC4\n84\t    criterion: \"cmd/base32 compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n85\t    traces:\n86\t      - R1.1\n87\t      - R1.2\n88\t      - R1.3\n89\t      - R1.4\n90\t      - R2.1\n91\t      - R2.2\n92\t      - R2.3\n93\t      - R2.4\n94\t      - R3.1\n95\t      - R3.2\n96\t      - R3.3\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00f3e8f9-5dfe-4b67-8534-b89b266d1d2d","uuid":"4a9c04ea-bc88-4788-ad80-f7bcb328c8b0","timestamp":"2026-05-23T02:41:21.210Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5509/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd079-base32.yaml","content":"id: srd079-base32\ntitle: \"cmd/base32: Base32 Encode and Decode\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship base32. Scripts that encode or decode Base32 data using the GNU\n  base32 format must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation must match\n  the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gbase32, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n  all flag combinations, using encoding/base32 from the Go standard library, verified\n  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Encode stdin or file contents to Base32 and write to stdout.\n  - G2: Decode Base32-encoded input back to binary with --decode (-d).\n  - G3: Support line wrapping control with --wrap (-w).\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gbase32 via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Encoding\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read from FILE or stdin (when no file or \"-\" is given) and encode the input using RFC 4648 Base32, writing the result to stdout.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must wrap encoded output at 76 characters per line by default.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-w COLS or --wrap=COLS must set the wrap column. -w 0 disables wrapping (single line output).\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when a named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Decoding\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-d or --decode must decode Base32 input from FILE or stdin and write the binary result to stdout.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must ignore whitespace (newlines, spaces) in the input during decoding.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-i or --ignore-garbage must ignore non-alphabet characters in the input during decoding.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 with an error to stderr when the input contains invalid Base32 characters (without --ignore-garbage).\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on successful encoding or decoding.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error (invalid input, missing file, invalid option).\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/base32 does not implement Base32hex (extended hex alphabet).\n  - cmd/base32 does not implement Base64; use base64 for that.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"echo hello | base32 produces Base32 encoded output matching gbase32.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"echo NBSWY3DP | base32 -d produces 'hello', matching gbase32 -d.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gbase32 passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/base32 compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
