{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (task #5509) from an automated code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The specific task is to implement `cmd/base32` - a Base32 encoding utility matching GNU coreutils behavior. The task scope is limited to srd079 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (the Encoding group only). Two files must be created: `cmd/base32/main.go` and `cmd/base32/base32_test.go`. The code must compile, pass `go vet`, and pass differential tests against the `gbase32` reference binary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - RFC 4648 Base32 encoding using Go's `encoding/base32.StdEncoding`\n   - Shared encoding library `pkg/encutil` with `Encode()`, `EncoderConfig`, and `OpenInput()` functions\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing framework `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU `gbase32`\n   - Line wrapping at 76 characters by default, configurable via `-w`/`--wrap` flag\n   - Graceful skip pattern when reference binary is not installed\n   - Copyright header requirement: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + SPDX\n   - No git commands allowed - git managed externally by orchestrator\n   - Write all files before compiling, no incremental build loops\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd079-base32.yaml` (READ)\n     - Contains the full SRD for base32 utility\n     - R1 (Encoding): R1.1 (read FILE/stdin, encode RFC 4648 Base32), R1.2 (wrap at 76 chars default), R1.3 (-w COLS/--wrap=COLS flag), R1.4 (exit 1 on file open error)\n     - R2 (Decoding): R2.1-R2.4 (NOT in scope for this task)\n     - R3 (Exit codes/SIGPIPE): R3.1-R3.3 (NOT explicitly in scope but D1 requires SIGPIPE handler)\n     - Non-goals: no Base32hex, no Base64\n     - Package contract imports: pkg/encutil, pkg/sys\n   \n   - `pkg/encutil/encode.go` (PROVIDED in context)\n     - Key function: `Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error`\n     - `EncoderConfig struct { Encode func([]byte) string; WrapCol int }`\n     - Handles line wrapping internally via `writeWrapped()`\n   \n   - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` (PROVIDED in context)\n     - `Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error`\n     - `DecoderConfig struct { Decode func(string) ([]byte, error); IgnoreGarbage bool }`\n     - `OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` - returns stdin for \"\" or \"-\"\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - installs SIGPIPE handler that exits 0\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` and `pkg/testutils/build.go` (PROVIDED in context)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - compiles cmd package, returns binary path\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` - runs differential tests\n     - `DiffTest` struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, ExitCode fields\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. No code has been written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand all requirements for base32\n   - Identified that task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only (encoding), but the utility needs basic flag parsing structure\n   - Identified all pkg/ dependencies and their contracts from the provided context\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed stitch task prompt containing full project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, coding standards, task requirements, design decisions, acceptance criteria, and constraints. The task is to implement cmd/base32 with srd079 R1.1-R1.4.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed conversation summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/base32/main.go` implementing srd079 R1.1-R1.4 (encoding functionality)\n   - Create `cmd/base32/base32_test.go` with differential tests against gbase32\n   - Run `go build -o bin/base32 ./cmd/base32/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/base32/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/base32/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`srd079-base32.yaml`) and was about to begin implementation. No code has been written yet. The implementation plan based on the SRD and design decisions is:\n\n   For `cmd/base32/main.go`:\n   - Copyright header\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main (D1)\n   - Parse flags: `-w`/`--wrap` (default 76), `-d`/`--decode`, `-i`/`--ignore-garbage`\n   - Use `encutil.OpenInput()` for file/stdin handling (D3)\n   - Use `encoding/base32.StdEncoding` for Base32 alphabet (D4)\n   - Use `encutil.Encode()` with `EncoderConfig{Encode: base32.StdEncoding.EncodeToString, WrapCol: wrapCol}` (D2)\n   - Exit 1 with stderr error on file open failure (R1.4)\n\n   For `cmd/base32/base32_test.go`:\n   - Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gbase32\")` (D5)\n   - Skip if gbase32 not found\n   - Test cases for: basic encoding, wrap at 76, custom wrap width, wrap 0, file input, missing file error\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/base32/main.go` and `cmd/base32/base32_test.go` in full, then compile and test. The task description states: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands.\" The specific requirements are srd079 R1.1 (encode from FILE/stdin), R1.2 (wrap at 76 default), R1.3 (-w COLS flag), R1.4 (exit 1 on file error). Design decisions D1-D5 specify the implementation approach using pkg/encutil and pkg/sys.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you genera